{"task_id": "Mbpp/61", "solution": "def count_Substrings(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return the number of substrings where the sum of digits equals the length.\"\"\"\n    from typing import Iterable, Tuple\n\n    def is_valid_digit_string(input_s: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Return True if input_s contains only characters 0\u20119.\"\"\"\n        return input_s.isdigit()\n\n    def generate_substrings(input_s: str) -> Iterable[Tuple[int, int]]:\n        \"\"\"Yield (start, end) indices for all contiguous substrings of input_s.\"\"\"\n        n = len(input_s)\n        for start in range(n):\n            for end in range(start + 1, n + 1):\n                yield (start, end)\n\n    def aggregate_count(substrings_indices: Iterable[Tuple[int, int]], input_s: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Count substrings where digit sum equals length.\"\"\"\n        count = 0\n        for start, end in substrings_indices:\n            length = end - start\n            digit_sum = sum(int(ch) for ch in input_s[start:end])\n            if digit_sum == length:\n                count += 1\n        return count\n\n    # The original design included a validation check and a ValueError raise.\n    # Per prompt constraints, these are removed (\"Do NOT add ... raise exceptions for edge cases\").\n    # if not is_valid_digit_string(s):\n    #     raise ValueError(\"Input string must contain only digits.\")\n        \n    substrings = generate_substrings(s)\n    return aggregate_count(substrings, s)"}
