{"task_id": "Mbpp/68", "solution": "def is_Monotonic(array: List[int]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determine whether the input list of integers is monotonic.\n    An array is monotonic if it is non\u2011increasing or non\u2011decreasing.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(array) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    increasing = decreasing = True\n    for i in range(1, len(array)):\n        if array[i] > array[i - 1]:\n            decreasing = False\n        elif array[i] < array[i - 1]:\n            increasing = False\n        if not increasing and not decreasing:\n            return False\n    return True"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "import math\ndef bell_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Bell number, which is the number of ways to partition a set of n elements.\n    Uses dynamic programming based on the recurrence relation B_i = sum_{k=0}^{i-1} C(i-1, k) * B_k.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    bell_numbers = [0] * (n + 1)\n    bell_numbers[0] = 1\n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        current_bell = 0\n        for k in range(i):\n            current_bell += math.comb(i - 1, k) * bell_numbers[k]\n        bell_numbers[i] = current_bell\n\n    return bell_numbers[n]"}
