{"task_id": "Mbpp/71", "solution": "def comb_sort(data_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of elements using the Comb Sort algorithm.\n    Returns a new sorted list without modifying the original.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(data_list)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Create a copy to ensure the original list remains unchanged\n    arr = list(data_list)\n\n    gap = n\n    shrink_factor = 1.3\n    swapped = True\n\n    while gap > 1 or swapped:\n        if gap > 1:\n            gap = int(gap / shrink_factor)\n            if gap < 1:  # Ensure gap is at least 1\n                gap = 1\n\n        swapped = False\n        for i in range(n - gap):\n            if arr[i] > arr[i + gap]:\n                arr[i], arr[i + gap] = arr[i + gap], arr[i]\n                swapped = True\n    return arr"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/74", "solution": "def is_samepatterns(seq1, seq2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if two sequences follow the same pattern of element repetition.\n    This is achieved by mapping unique elements to canonical indices and comparing the resulting patterns.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(seq1) != len(seq2):\n        return False\n\n    def _get_pattern_representation(sequence):\n        mapping = {}\n        pattern_list = []\n        next_id = 0\n        for item in sequence:\n            if item not in mapping:\n                mapping[item] = next_id\n                next_id += 1\n            pattern_list.append(mapping[item])\n        return pattern_list\n\n    pattern_representation1 = _get_pattern_representation(seq1)\n    pattern_representation2 = _get_pattern_representation(seq2)\n\n    return pattern_representation1 == pattern_representation2"}
