{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "def is_undulating(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if the number's digits strictly alternate between increasing and decreasing. Handles negative numbers by using their absolute value.\"\"\"\n    digits = [int(d) for d in str(abs(number))]\n    if len(digits) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    direction = None\n    for i in range(1, len(digits)):\n        if digits[i] == digits[i - 1]:\n            return False\n        if digits[i] > digits[i - 1]:\n            current = 'up'\n        else:\n            current = 'down'\n\n        if direction is None:\n            direction = current\n        else:\n            if current == direction:\n                return False\n            direction = current\n\n    return True"}
