{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "def eulerian_num(n, m):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the Eulerian number a(n, m) using the combinatorial formula.\n    Assumes n and m are non-negative integers with m < n.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _factorial(val):\n        \"\"\"Calculates the factorial of a non-negative integer.\"\"\"\n        res = 1\n        for i in range(1, val + 1):\n            res *= i\n        return res\n\n    def _combinations(n_val, k_val):\n        \"\"\"Calculates C(n_val, k_val), the number of combinations.\"\"\"\n        if k_val < 0 or k_val > n_val:\n            return 0\n        if k_val == 0 or k_val == n_val:\n            return 1\n        if k_val > n_val // 2:\n            k_val = n_val - k_val\n        return _factorial(n_val) // (_factorial(k_val) * _factorial(n_val - k_val))\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for k in range(m + 1):\n        term = ((-1)**k) * _combinations(n + 1, k) * ((m + 1 - k)**n)\n        total_sum += term\n\n    return total_sum"}
