{"task_id": "Mbpp/119", "solution": "def search(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the element that appears only once in a sorted array where all other elements appear twice.\n    Assumes valid input: sorted array with an odd length and a single unique element.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(arr) - 1\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n\n        # Check if mid is part of a pair\n        if arr[mid] == arr[mid ^ 1]:  # mid ^ 1 will give the other index of the pair\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid\n\n    return arr[low]"}
