{"task_id": "Mbpp/123", "solution": "def amicable_numbers_sum(limit: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all amicable numbers from 1 up to the specified limit.\n    An amicable pair (a, b) consists of two distinct numbers where the sum\n    of proper divisors of a is b, and the sum of proper divisors of b is a.\n    \"\"\"\n    if limit < 1:\n        return 0\n\n    # Stores the sum of proper divisors for each number up to 'limit'.\n    # divisor_sum[i] will hold the sum of all divisors of 'i' excluding 'i' itself.\n    divisor_sum = [0] * (limit + 1)\n\n    # Pre-compute sum of proper divisors using a sieve-like approach.\n    # For each number 'i' (potential divisor), iterate through its multiples 'j'.\n    for i in range(1, limit):\n        for j in range(2 * i, limit + 1, i):\n            divisor_sum[j] += i\n\n    total_amicable_sum = 0\n\n    # Identify amicable pairs and accumulate their sum.\n    # For each number 'n', check if it forms an amicable pair.\n    for n in range(1, limit + 1):\n        s = divisor_sum[n] # s is the sum of proper divisors of n.\n\n        # An amicable pair (n, s) must satisfy three conditions:\n        # 1. s > n: Ensures n and s are distinct and we only process each pair once\n        #    (n will always be the smaller number in the pair).\n        # 2. s <= limit: Both numbers in the pair must be within the specified limit.\n        # 3. divisor_sum[s] == n: The sum of proper divisors of s must equal n.\n        if s > n and s <= limit and divisor_sum[s] == n:\n            total_amicable_sum += n + s\n\n    return total_amicable_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/125", "solution": "def find_length(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum difference between the number of 0s and 1s in any substring.\n    Applies Kadane's algorithm by treating '0' as +1 and '1' as -1.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_so_far = 0\n    current_max = 0\n    for char in s:\n        if char == '0':\n            current_max += 1\n        elif char == '1':\n            current_max -= 1\n        \n        # If current_max becomes negative, reset it to 0\n        # as a negative prefix will only reduce future sums.\n        if current_max < 0:\n            current_max = 0\n        \n        # Update the overall maximum\n        max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n            \n    return max_so_far"}
