{"task_id": "Mbpp/129", "solution": "def magic_square_test(matrix: list[list[int]]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given matrix is a magic square.\n    A magic square has equal sums for all rows, columns, and both main diagonals.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(matrix)\n\n    # An empty matrix or a non-square matrix cannot be a magic square.\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    # Verify that the matrix is square (all rows have n columns).\n    for row in matrix:\n        if len(row) != n:\n            return False\n\n    # A 1x1 matrix is always a magic square.\n    if n == 1:\n        return True\n\n    # Calculate the target sum from the first row.\n    target_sum = sum(matrix[0])\n\n    # Check all row sums.\n    for i in range(n):\n        if sum(matrix[i]) != target_sum:\n            return False\n\n    # Check all column sums.\n    for j in range(n):\n        current_col_sum = 0\n        for i in range(n):\n            current_col_sum += matrix[i][j]\n        if current_col_sum != target_sum:\n            return False\n\n    # Check the main diagonal sum (top-left to bottom-right).\n    main_diag_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        main_diag_sum += matrix[i][i]\n    if main_diag_sum != target_sum:\n        return False\n\n    # Check the anti-diagonal sum (top-right to bottom-left).\n    anti_diag_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        anti_diag_sum += matrix[i][n - 1 - i]\n    if anti_diag_sum != target_sum:\n        return False\n\n    # If all checks pass, the matrix is a magic square.\n    return True"}
