{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "def pancake_sort(elements):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of elements using the pancake sort algorithm.\n    Returns a new sorted list, leaving the original unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _flip(arr, start, end):\n        \"\"\"Reverses the sub-array arr[start:end+1] in-place.\"\"\"\n        while start < end:\n            arr[start], arr[end] = arr[end], arr[start]\n            start += 1\n            end -= 1\n\n    def _index_of_max(arr, start, end):\n        \"\"\"Finds the index of the maximum element in arr[start:end+1].\"\"\"\n        max_val = arr[start]\n        max_idx = start\n        for i in range(start + 1, end + 1):\n            if arr[i] > max_val:\n                max_val = arr[i]\n                max_idx = i\n        return max_idx\n\n    # Work on a copy to preserve the original list\n    arr = list(elements)\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    # Iterate from the end of the array to the beginning\n    # `current_size` represents the unsorted portion of the array.\n    for current_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        # Find the index of the maximum element in arr[0...current_size-1]\n        max_idx = _index_of_max(arr, 0, current_size - 1)\n\n        # If the maximum element is not already at its correct position\n        if max_idx != current_size - 1:\n            # 1. Flip the prefix from 0 to max_idx to bring the max element to the front\n            _flip(arr, 0, max_idx)\n\n            # 2. Flip the prefix from 0 to current_size-1 to move the max element\n            #    to its final sorted position in the current window\n            _flip(arr, 0, current_size - 1)\n\n    return arr"}
