{"task_id": "Mbpp/145", "solution": "def max_Abs_Diff(sequence):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum difference between any two elements in a given sequence.\n    Returns 0 if the sequence has fewer than two elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    it = iter(sequence)\n    try:\n        min_val = next(it)\n        max_val = min_val\n    except StopIteration:\n        return 0  # Sequence is empty\n\n    for val in it:\n        if val < min_val:\n            min_val = val\n        elif val > max_val:\n            max_val = val\n\n    return max_val - min_val"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/160", "solution": "def extended_euclidean_algorithm(a: int, b: int) -> Tuple[int, int, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes (x, y, g) such that ax + by = g, where g is gcd(a, b).\n    This function implements the extended Euclidean algorithm recursively.\n    \"\"\"\n    if b == 0:\n        return 1, 0, a\n    \n    x1, y1, g = extended_euclidean_algorithm(b, a % b)\n    x = y1\n    y = x1 - (a // b) * y1\n    return x, y, g\ndef find_solution(a: int, b: int, n: int) -> Optional[Tuple[int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns integers x and y that satisfy ax + by = n as a tuple,\n    or returns None if no solution exists.\n    \"\"\"\n    # If both a and b are zero:\n    # If n is also zero, there are infinitely many solutions (any x, y works).\n    # If n is not zero, there are no solutions.\n    # The design specifies returning None for a=0, b=0 case.\n    if a == 0 and b == 0:\n        return None\n\n    # Use the extended Euclidean algorithm to find a particular solution (x0, y0)\n    # for the equation a*x0 + b*y0 = g, where g = gcd(a, b).\n    x0, y0, g = extended_euclidean_algorithm(a, b)\n\n    # A solution to ax + by = n exists if and only if n is divisible by gcd(a, b).\n    if n % g != 0:\n        return None\n\n    # Scale the particular solution (x0, y0) to find a solution for ax + by = n.\n    # The scaling factor is n / g.\n    k = n // g\n    return (x0 * k, y0 * k)"}
