{"task_id": "Mbpp/170", "solution": "def sum_range_list(elements: list, start: int, end: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Public fa\u00e7ade that validates input, constructs domain objects,\n    and delegates calculation to SumCalculator.\n    \"\"\"\n    class NumberList:\n        def __init__(self, elements: list):\n            self.elements = elements\n\n    class IndexRange:\n        def __init__(self, start: int, end: int):\n            self.start = start\n            self.end = end\n\n    class SumCalculator:\n        def calculate(self, number_list, index_range):\n            elements = number_list.elements\n            start, end = index_range.start, index_range.end\n\n            if not elements:\n                return 0\n\n            # Normalize negative indices per Python semantics.\n            start = start if start >= 0 else len(elements) + start\n            end = end if end >= 0 else len(elements) + end\n\n            # Validate bounds and start <= end.\n            if start < 0 or end >= len(elements) or start > end:\n                raise IndexError(\"Index out of bounds or start index is greater than end index.\")\n\n            # Compute inclusive sum using slicing.\n            return sum(elements[start : end + 1])\n\n    number_list_obj = NumberList(elements)\n    index_range_obj = IndexRange(start, end)\n    calculator = SumCalculator()\n    return calculator.calculate(number_list_obj, index_range_obj)"}
