{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "import functools\ndef get_total_number_of_sequences(m: int, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the total number of sequences of length n.\n    Each element must be a positive integer, >= twice the previous, and <= m.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    @functools.lru_cache(None)\n    def _count_sequences(last_val: int, length_left: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Recursively counts valid sequences starting from `last_val`\n        with `length_left` elements remaining.\n        \"\"\"\n        if length_left == 0:\n            return 1\n\n        count = 0\n        min_next_val = 2 * last_val\n        for next_val in range(min_next_val, m + 1):\n            count += _count_sequences(next_val, length_left - 1)\n        return count\n\n    total_sequences = 0\n    # The first element of the sequence can be any integer from 1 to m.\n    # We then recursively count sequences for the remaining n-1 elements.\n    for first_val in range(1, m + 1):\n        total_sequences += _count_sequences(first_val, n - 1)\n\n    return total_sequences"}
