{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "def lps(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the length of the longest palindromic subsequence in the given string.\n    Uses dynamic programming with O(n^2) time and space complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of the longest palindromic subsequence\n    # for the substring s[i...j].\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # All substrings of length 1 have an LPS length of 1.\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table for substrings of increasing length.\n    for length in range(2, n + 1):\n        # Iterate through all possible starting indices for the current length.\n        for i in range(n - length + 1):\n            j = i + length - 1  # Calculate the corresponding ending index.\n            if s[i] == s[j]:\n                # If the characters at the ends match, they contribute 2 to the LPS.\n                # The remaining LPS comes from the inner substring s[i+1...j-1].\n                dp[i][j] = 2 + dp[i + 1][j - 1]\n            else:\n                # If the characters at the ends don't match, we exclude one character\n                # and take the maximum LPS from the two resulting substrings.\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i + 1][j], dp[i][j - 1])\n\n    return dp[0][n - 1]"}
