{"task_id": "Mbpp/255", "solution": "import itertools\nfrom typing import List, Tuple\ndef combinations_colors(elements: List[str], n: int) -> List[Tuple[str, ...]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates all length-n combinations with repetition from a list of elements.\n    Returns a list of tuples, each representing a combination.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Handle negative n: return an empty list as exceptions are not allowed per requirements.\n    if n < 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Handle n == 0: return a list containing a single empty tuple.\n    if n == 0:\n        return [()]\n\n    # Handle empty input list for n > 0: return an empty list.\n    if not elements:\n        return []\n\n    # Generate combinations using itertools.product, which handles repetition.\n    return list(itertools.product(elements, repeat=n))"}
