{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "def count_Primes_nums(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the number of prime numbers strictly less than the given non-negative number.\n    Uses the Sieve of Eratosthenes algorithm for efficient prime counting.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 2:\n        return 0\n\n    is_prime = [True] * n\n    is_prime[0] = False\n    is_prime[1] = False\n\n    for i in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n        if is_prime[i]:\n            for j in range(i*i, n, i):\n                is_prime[j] = False\n\n    return sum(is_prime)"}
