{"task_id": "Mbpp/270", "solution": "def sum_even_and_even_index(elements: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the sum of all even numbers that appear at even indices (0-based) in a list.\n    Assumes `elements` is a list of integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    total = 0\n    for idx in range(0, len(elements), 2):  # Iterate through even indices only\n        val = elements[idx]\n        if val % 2 == 0:  # Check if the number at the even index is also even\n            total += val\n    return total"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/271", "solution": "def even_Power_Sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the first n even natural numbers raised to the fifth power.\n    This implementation follows a component-based design with dedicated classes.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    class EvenNumber:\n        \"\"\"Represents an even natural number.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, value: int):\n            self.value = value\n\n    class PowerSumCalculator:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of powers of even numbers up to n.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, n_val: int):\n            self.n = n_val\n\n        def computeSum(self) -> int:\n            \"\"\"Computes the sum of the first n even numbers raised to the fifth power.\"\"\"\n            total_sum = 0\n            for i in range(1, self.n + 1):\n                even_number_obj = EvenNumber(2 * i)\n                total_sum += even_number_obj.value ** 5\n            return total_sum\n\n    calculator = PowerSumCalculator(n)\n    return calculator.computeSum()"}
