{"task_id": "Mbpp/276", "solution": "import math\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nclass MathLibrary:\n    \"\"\"Provides mathematical constants.\"\"\"\n    pi: float = math.pi\nclass VolumeCalculator:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the volume of a Cylinder.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, math_lib: MathLibrary = MathLibrary()):\n        self.math_lib = math_lib\n\n    def calculate_volume(self, cylinder: Cylinder) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Return V = \u03c0 * r^2 * h.\"\"\"\n        return self.math_lib.pi * (cylinder.radius ** 2) * cylinder.height\ndef volume_cylinder(radius: float, height: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute the volume of a right circular cylinder.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    radius : float\n        Non\u2011negative radius of the cylinder.\n    height : float\n        Non\u2011negative height of the cylinder.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    float\n        The volume V = \u03c0 * r^2 * h.\n\n    Raises\n    ------\n    ValueError\n        If radius or height is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if radius < 0 or height < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Radius and height must be non\u2011negative.\")\n    cylinder = Cylinder(radius, height)\n    calculator = VolumeCalculator()\n    return calculator.calculate_volume(cylinder)"}
