{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "import math\ndef max_sub_array_sum_repeated(array: list[int], k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest sum of a contiguous subarray in a modified array,\n    formed by repeating the given array k times.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(array)\n\n    # Helper function for Kadane's algorithm on a single array.\n    # Handles cases with all negative numbers correctly.\n    def kadane(arr):\n        max_so_far = arr[0]\n        current_max = arr[0]\n        for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n            current_max = max(arr[i], current_max + arr[i])\n            max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n        return max_so_far\n\n    # If k is 1, the problem reduces to standard Kadane's on the original array.\n    if k == 1:\n        return kadane(array)\n\n    # Calculate maximum subarray sum within a single instance of the array.\n    max_sum_in_one_array = kadane(array)\n\n    # Calculate the total sum of the original array.\n    total_array_sum = sum(array)\n\n    # Calculate the maximum sum of a prefix of the original array.\n    max_prefix_sum = -math.inf\n    current_prefix_sum = 0\n    for x in array:\n        current_prefix_sum += x\n        max_prefix_sum = max(max_prefix_sum, current_prefix_sum)\n\n    # Calculate the maximum sum of a suffix of the original array.\n    max_suffix_sum = -math.inf\n    current_suffix_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        current_suffix_sum += array[i]\n        max_suffix_sum = max(max_suffix_sum, current_suffix_sum)\n\n    # Initialize result with the best sum found within a single array.\n    ans = max_sum_in_one_array\n\n    # Consider subarrays that span across the boundary of two repetitions.\n    # This involves the maximum suffix sum of the first array and max prefix sum of the second.\n    ans = max(ans, max_suffix_sum + max_prefix_sum)\n\n    # If the total array sum is positive, adding full arrays in between can increase the sum.\n    # This applies when k > 2, as (k-2) represents the number of full arrays between suffix and prefix.\n    if total_array_sum > 0 and k > 2:\n        ans = max(ans, max_suffix_sum + (k - 2) * total_array_sum + max_prefix_sum)\n\n    return int(ans)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/290", "solution": "def max_length(list_of_lists):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return the maximum length and the first sub-list of that length.\n\n    Returns a tuple where the first element is the maximum length (int) and the second\n    element is the first sub-list of that length (list) or None if the input list is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_len = 0\n    max_sublist = None\n\n    for sub in list_of_lists:\n        current_len = len(sub)\n        if current_len > max_len:\n            max_len = current_len\n            max_sublist = list(sub)\n\n    return max_len, max_sublist"}
