{"task_id": "Mbpp/448", "solution": "def cal_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of Perrin numbers from P(0) to P(n) inclusive.\"\"\"\n    \n    if n == 0:\n        return 3\n\n    if n == 1:\n        return 3\n\n    if n == 2:\n        return 5\n\n    # Initialize with the first three Perrin numbers and their sum\n    # P(0), P(1), P(2)\n    p_minus3 = 3\n    p_minus2 = 0\n    p_minus1 = 2\n    total_sum = 5 # Sum of P(0), P(1), P(2)\n\n    # Iteratively calculate subsequent Perrin numbers and add to the total sum\n    for _ in range(3, n + 1):\n        current_perrin = p_minus2 + p_minus3\n        total_sum += current_perrin\n\n        # Shift values for the next iteration: p(i-3) becomes p(i-2), etc.\n        p_minus3 = p_minus2\n        p_minus2 = p_minus1\n        p_minus1 = current_perrin\n    \n    return total_sum"}
