{"task_id": "Mbpp/589", "solution": "def perfect_squares(start: int, end: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds perfect squares between two given numbers (inclusive).\n    The squares are returned in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    perfect_sq_list = []\n    # Calculate the integer square root of the lower bound.\n    # We must handle cases where start is 0 or positive.\n    # The smallest possible square root for positive integers is 1.\n    start_root = int(start**0.5) if start >= 0 else 0\n    if start < 0 and end < 0: # If both are negative, no perfect squares\n        return []\n\n    # Calculate the integer square root of the upper bound.\n    end_root = int(end**0.5) if end >= 0 else 0\n\n    # Iterate from the calculated starting root up to the ending root (inclusive).\n    # We ensure the loop starts at 0 if start is very small and includes 0 as a perfect square.\n    for i in range(start_root, end_root + 1):\n        square = i * i\n        # Only add the square if it falls within the specified range [start, end]\n        # and ensure it's not negative if start/end allow it.\n        if square >= start and square <= end:\n            perfect_sq_list.append(square)\n\n    return perfect_sq_list"}
