{"task_id": "Mbpp/594", "solution": "def diff_even_odd(numbers: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the difference of the first even and first odd number of a given list.\n    Raises ValueError if either an even or an odd number is not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_even = None\n    first_odd = None\n\n    for num in numbers:\n        if first_even is None and num % 2 == 0:\n            first_even = num\n        if first_odd is None and num % 2 != 0:\n            first_odd = num\n        if first_even is not None and first_odd is not None:\n            break\n\n    if first_even is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"The list does not contain an even number.\")\n    if first_odd is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"The list does not contain an odd number.\")\n\n    return first_even - first_odd"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/592", "solution": "import math\ndef sum_Of_product(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the product of consecutive binomial coefficients for a given n.\n    This function computes Sum(C(n, k) * C(n, k+1)) for k from 0 to n-1.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    for k in range(n):\n        coeff_k = math.comb(n, k)\n        coeff_k_plus_1 = math.comb(n, k + 1)\n        total_sum += coeff_k * coeff_k_plus_1\n    return total_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/598", "solution": "def armstrong_number(number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a number is an Armstrong number.\n    An Armstrong number is one whose sum of digits raised to the power of the number of digits equals the number itself.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        return False\n\n    num_str = str(number)\n    n = len(num_str)\n    armstrong_sum = 0\n    for digit_char in num_str:\n        armstrong_sum += int(digit_char) ** n\n    return armstrong_sum == number"}
