{"task_id": "Mbpp/615", "solution": "def average_tuple(tuple_of_tuples: tuple[tuple[float, ...], ...]) -> list[float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the average value for each inner tuple within a tuple of tuples.\n    Returns a list of these averages.\n    \"\"\"\n    averages = []\n    for inner_tuple in tuple_of_tuples:\n        if inner_tuple:  # Avoid division by zero for empty tuples\n            average = sum(inner_tuple) / len(inner_tuple)\n            averages.append(average)\n        else:\n            averages.append(0.0) # Or handle as per specific empty tuple requirement, defaulting to 0.0 here\n    return averages"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/616", "solution": "from typing import Tuple\ndef tuple_modulo(tuple1: Tuple[int, ...], tuple2: Tuple[int, ...]) -> Tuple[int, ...]:\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input tuples must have the same length.\")\n    result = []\n    for a, b in zip(tuple1, tuple2):\n        if b == 0:\n            raise ZeroDivisionError(\"Modulo by zero is undefined.\")\n        result.append(a % b)\n    return tuple(result)"}
