{"task_id": "Mbpp/630", "solution": "from typing import List, Tuple\ndef get_coordinates(coord: Tuple[int, int]) -> List[List[int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts all 9 adjacent coordinates (including itself) for a given coordinate.\n    The output is a 3x3 grid in row-major order, starting from the top-left neighbor.\n    \"\"\"\n    x, y = coord\n    adjacent_coords = []\n    for dx in range(-1, 2):  # Iterate x-offsets (-1, 0, 1)\n        current_x = x + dx\n        for dy in range(-1, 2):  # Iterate y-offsets (-1, 0, 1)\n            current_y = y + dy\n            adjacent_coords.append([current_x, current_y])\n    return adjacent_coords"}
