{"task_id": "Mbpp/638", "solution": "import math\ndef wind_chill(wind_speed_kmh: float, temperature_c: float) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the wind chill index using the standard Celsius formula.\n    The result is rounded to the nearest integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Wind Chill Index formula for Celsius (Environment Canada standard)\n    # WCI = 13.12 + 0.6215*T - 11.37*V^0.16 + 0.3965*T*V^0.16\n    # Where T = temperature in Celsius and V = wind velocity in km/h.\n    \n    wind_chill_index = (\n        13.12\n        + 0.6215 * temperature_c\n        - 11.37 * (wind_speed_kmh ** 0.16)\n        + 0.3965 * temperature_c * (wind_speed_kmh ** 0.16)\n    )\n    \n    # Round to the nearest integer, as implied by the assertion wind_chill(120,35)==40\n    return round(wind_chill_index)"}
