{"task_id": "Mbpp/721", "solution": "def maxAverageOfPath(matrix):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a square matrix, finds the path from top-left to bottom-right\n    moving only right or down, that has the maximum average cost.\n    Since all such paths have the same length (2N-1), this is equivalent\n    to finding the path with the maximum total cost.\n    \"\"\"\n    class Cell:\n        def __init__(self, row, col, cost):\n            self.row = row\n            self.col = col\n            self.cost = cost\n\n    class Path:\n        def __init__(self, cells):\n            self.cells = cells\n            self.totalCost = sum(cell.cost for cell in cells)\n            self.length = len(cells)\n\n        def average(self):\n            return self.totalCost / self.length\n\n    class Matrix:\n        def __init__(self, cells_data):\n            # As per design, assuming valid matrix input without explicit checks here.\n            self.size = len(cells_data)\n            self.cells = cells_data\n\n    class PathCalculator:\n        def __init__(self, matrix_obj):\n            self.matrix = matrix_obj\n\n        def computeMaxAveragePath(self):\n            n = self.matrix.size\n            cells_data = self.matrix.cells\n\n            # dp[i][j] stores the maximum sum of costs to reach cell (i, j)\n            dp = [[0.0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n            # Initialize the top-left cell\n            dp[0][0] = float(cells_data[0][0])\n\n            # Fill the first row\n            for j in range(1, n):\n                dp[0][j] = dp[0][j-1] + cells_data[0][j]\n\n            # Fill the first column\n            for i in range(1, n):\n                dp[i][0] = dp[i-1][0] + cells_data[i][0]\n\n            # Fill the rest of the dp table\n            for i in range(1, n):\n                for j in range(1, n):\n                    dp[i][j] = max(dp[i-1][j], dp[i][j-1]) + cells_data[i][j]\n\n            # Reconstruct the path with the maximum sum from bottom-right to top-left\n            i, j = n - 1, n - 1\n            path_cells_list = []\n            \n            while i >= 0 and j >= 0:\n                path_cells_list.append(Cell(i, j, cells_data[i][j]))\n                if i == 0 and j == 0:\n                    break\n                \n                if i == 0:\n                    j -= 1\n                elif j == 0:\n                    i -= 1\n                else:\n                    if dp[i-1][j] > dp[i][j-1]:\n                        i -= 1\n                    else:\n                        j -= 1\n            \n            path_cells_list.reverse() # Reverse to get path from start to end\n            \n            final_path = Path(path_cells_list)\n            return final_path.average()\n\n    # Main logic of the maxAverageOfPath function\n    matrix_instance = Matrix(matrix)\n    calculator = PathCalculator(matrix_instance)\n    return calculator.computeMaxAveragePath()"}
