{"task_id": "Mbpp/809", "solution": "def check_smaller(tuple1, tuple2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if each element of the second tuple is smaller than its\n    corresponding element in the first tuple.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        return False\n    \n    for a, b in zip(tuple1, tuple2):\n        if not (b < a):\n            return False\n            \n    return True"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/430", "solution": "def parabola_directrix(a, b, c):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the y-coordinate of the directrix for a parabola defined by y = ax^2 + bx + c.\n    This uses the formula: d = c - (b^2 / (4a)) - (1 / (4a)).\n    \"\"\"\n    # Compute the directrix value based on the standard formula for a vertical parabola.\n    # Division by zero for a=0 is not explicitly handled as per design constraints.\n    directrix_value = c - (b**2 / (4 * a)) - (1 / (4 * a))\n    return directrix_value"}
